  "sample": {
    "description": "Balanced panel of 71 small open economies with complete WDI national accounts (changes in inventories, GDP, GFCF, private and government consumption, exports, imports, population) 1993-2022; groups: 24 advanced, 13 high-income EM, 24 middle-income EM, 10 low-income EM. 1 country(ies) from paper's 72 excluded due to incomplete current WDI vintage (no imputation). Detailed missing listed in differences.",
    "n": 71,
    "start": "1993-01-01",
    "end": "2022-12-31",
    "same_as_paper": false,
    "missing": 1,
    "extra": 0,
    "differences": "Current WDI vintage 2026-10-08 missing vs paper vintage 1993-2022 complete records for 72: RUS (high): C_K missing [1993, 1994, 1995]; X_K missing [2022]; M_K missing [2022]. Paper groups were 24 advanced, 14 high-income EM, 24 middle-income EM, 10 low-income EM; current complete panel has advanced 24, high 13, middle 24, low 10. RUS in high-income EM group absent (NE.CON.PRVT.KN 1993-1995, NE.EXP.GNFS.KN and NE.IMP.GNFS.KN 2022). No proxy/imputation used - strict paper definition of complete records applied.",
    "cannot_count": "",
    "not_rebuilt": {},
    "substitutions": "Data vintage WDI 2026-10-08 via api.worldbank.org; GDP trend via country-specific log-quadratic regression; inventory ratio delta_INV/Ytrend_{t-1} filtered via country-specific quadratic trend in levels; per-capita log-differences for GDP, consumption, investment, government, exports, imports; median across countries for group statistics as per paper Table 2. No proxy substitution - strict complete-records filter; current vintage differs from paper vintage in RUS data availability."
  },
  "notes": "Sample built from WDI indicators NE.GDI.STKB.CN, NY.GDP.MKTP.CN/KN, NE.GDI.FTOT.KN, NE.CON.PRVT.KN/CN, NE.CON.GOVT.KN, NE.EXP.GNFS.KN/CN, NE.IMP.GNFS.KN/CN, SP.POP.TOTL. Data fetched in batches with per_page=1000 pagination; balanced panel requires all 30 years non-missing. Russia 1993-1995 private consumption constant (NE.CON.PRVT.KN) and 2022 exports/imports constant (NE.EXP.GNFS.KN, NE.IMP.GNFS.KN) missing in current WDI vintage 2026-10-08, preventing a 72-country balanced panel on strictly complete records; current replication therefore uses 71 countries (24 advanced, 13 high-income EM, 24 middle-income EM, 10 low-income EM) with no imputation, so results are computed only from observed data as required. GDP trend obtained via country-specific log-quadratic regression log(Y_t)=beta0+beta1*t+beta2*t^2, t=0..29; Y_trend_{t-1}=exp(beta0+beta1*(t-1)+beta2*(t-1)^2). Ratio delta_INV/Y_trend_{t-1} filtered via country-specific quadratic regression ratio=beta0+beta1*t+beta2*t^2+eps; eps is delta_inv_c (cyclical). Volatility = country standard deviation (ddof=1) of delta_inv_c; median across countries per group (paper Figure discussion). Correlations, relative volatilities, autocorrelations computed per country then median across group (paper Table 2; Appendix C confirms median aggregation). Correlations align delta_inv_c[1:] (1994-2022) with log-diff per-capita aggregates (29 obs per country). Relative volatility = sd(delta_inv_c[1:]) / sd(delta growth aggregate). Autocorr = corr(delta_inv_c[1:], delta_inv_c[:-1]). SE reported as std of country-level estimates / sqrt(n_countries); for correlations etc n_obs pooled given as 29*countries. Unit-root/cointegration, LP impulse responses and variance shares not replicated due to data vintage and instrument requirements; only stylized facts fully reproducible from public WDI."
}